Chitin-Skank
Ingredients: BIT MUSIC (CHIPTUNE) + SKA + VIBRANT, TROPICAL & SUNNY + Lead Vocal + 1990s ERA
Creative Catalyst: Reverse-engineered from a saltwater-corroded 1996 cassette discovered inside a beachfront municipality time capsule.

Chitin-Skank sounds like a hyperactive third-wave ska band falling down a flight of stairs inside a giant, sun-drenched Nintendo Game Boy. Blistering live brass fanfares and syncopated clean guitar upstrokes violently interlock with chirping 4-bit square-wave leads, warbling tape-drag microtones, and rattling steel pans, all crowned by brassy, sunburnt lead vocals delivering irrepressible carnival hooks.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 168–192 BPM. Relentless 2-Tone skank accents firing on the upbeats, driven by hyperactive sixteenth-note noise-channel hi-hats, a galloping kick drum, and syncopated snare cracks.
- Harmonic Palette: Sun-bleached Major keys, Mixolydian calypso vamps (I–IV–V and I–vi–ii–V), and joyous brass voicings, constantly warped by microtonally detuned 8-bit arpeggios simulating tape-flutter and dying console battery voltage.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Bit-Spliced Skank Guitars: Classic Fender Stratocaster offbeat chops hard-clamped through 4-bit downsamplers, turning rhythmic guitar scratches into percussive insect chitters.
  2. Ferrite Flutter Horns: Full brass sections (trumpet, trombone, tenor sax) hot-tracked onto saturated cassette tape running through modulated motor-speed drifts, yielding seasick, sun-baked horn blasts.
  3. DMG Square-Wave Walking Bass: Low-end walking basslines routed through an original 1989 Game Boy DMG pulse channel, delivering a buzzy, rounded sub-bounce that slaps beneath the drums.
- Dynamics: Explosive and unstoppably sunny; manic verse-skanks drop abruptly into stuttering 8-bit breakdown chitters before detonating into wall-of-sound horn choruses and shouted gang refrains.

